    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## WordPress Blogs Published -> Marketing Engine\n\n**What it does:** Pulls published posts from the public WordPress REST API, counts how many were published each week (Monday-dated), and upserts that count into **Marketing Engine -> Blogs Published**, matched on **Week Key** (text). Only the Blogs Published field is touched; other Marketing Engine fields are left intact.\n\n**Setup:** No credential needed for WordPress (published posts are public). Airtable uses the existing **n8n SAMPLE OS Integration** token.\n\n**Caveats:**\n- WP returns max 100 posts per page. If the site ever exceeds 100 posts, add pagination (page param / Link header) on *WordPress: Get Posts*.\n- Week start = Monday (matches WF5). The upsert matches on the **Week Key** text field (date-field matching is unreliable in Airtable upsert).",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 440
      },
      "id": "EXAMPLE_UUID_02035426E2",
      "name": "Setup Notes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1264,
        848
      ]
